-bahl"],["socks","yangmal","YAHNG-mahl"],["jacket","jaket","JAH-ket"],["coat","koteu","KOH-teu"],["hat","moja","MOH-jah"],["glasses","angyeong","AHN-gyuhng"],["bag","gabang","gah-BAHNG"],["pocket","jumeoni","JOO-muh-nee"]]},{"id":"town","title":"Town","items":[["street","geori","guh-REE"],["shop","gage","GAH-geh"],["market","sijang","SHEE-jahng"],["bank","eunhaeng","EUN-haeng"],["hospital","byeongwon","BYUHNG-wuhn"],["school","hakgyo","HAHK-gyoh"],["station","yeok","yuhk"],["airport","gonghang","GOHNG-hahng"],["bus","beoseu","BUH-seu"],["train","gicha","GEE-chah"],["car","jadongcha","JAH-dohng-chah"],["bicycle","jajeongeo","JAH-juhn-guh"],["taxi","taeksi","TAEK-shee"],["restaurant","sikdang","SHEEK-dahng"],["bridge","dari","DAH-ree"],["park","gongwon","GOHNG-wuhn"]]},{"id":"time","title":"Time","items":[["day","nal","nahl"],["night","bam","bahm"],["morning","achim","AH-cheem"],["afternoon","ohu","OH-hoo"],["week","ju","joo"],["month","dal","dahl"],["year","nyeon","nyuhn"],["Monday","woryoil","WUH-ryoh-eel"],["Tuesday","hwayoil","HWAH-yoh-eel"],["Wednesday","suyoil","SOO-yoh-eel"],["Thursday","mogyoil","MOH-gyoh-eel"],["Friday","geumyoil","GEUM-yoh-eel"],["Saturday","toyoil","TOH-yoh-eel"],["Sunday","iryoil","EE-ryoh-eel"],["January","irwol","EE-rwuhl"],["summer","yeoreum","YUH-reum"],["winter","gyeoul","GYUH-ool"]]},{"id":"weather-and-nature","title":"Weather and nature","items":[["sun","haet-sal","HAET-sahl"],["rain","bi","bee"],["snow","nun","noon"],["wind","baram","BAH-rahm"],["cloud","gureum","GOO-reum"],["hot","deowoyo","DUH-woh-yoh"],["cold","chuwoyo","CHOO-woh-yoh"],["sea","bada","BAH-dah"],["river","gang","gahng"],["mountain","san","sahn"],["tree","namu","NAH-moo"],["flower","kkot","kkoht"],["sky","haneul","HAH-neul"]]},{"id":"work-and-school","title":"Work and school","items":[["teacher","seonsaengnim","SUHN-saeng-neem"],["student","haksaeng","HAHK-saeng"],["book","chaek","chaek"],["pen","pen","pen"],["pencil","yeonpil","YUHN-peel"],["paper","jong-i","JOHNG-ee"],["computer","keompyuteo","KUHM-pyoo-tuh"],["phone","jeonhwa","JUHN-hwah"],["work","il","eel"],["office","samusil","SAH-moo-sheel"],["doctor","uisa","EE-sah"],["police officer","gyeongchal","GYUHNG-chahl"],["lesson","suieop","SOO-uhp"],["exam","siheom","SHEE-huhm"]]},{"id":"describing","title":"Describing","items":[["big","keoyo","KUH-yoh"],["small","jagayo","JAH-gah-yoh"],["good","joayo","JOH-ah-yoh"],["bad","nappayo","NAH-ppah-yoh"],["new","saeroun","SAE-roh-oon"],["old","oraedoen","OH-rae-dwen"],["beautiful","yeppeoyo","YEH-ppuh-yoh"],["ugly","mot saenggyeosseoyo","moht saeng-gyuh-suh-yoh"],["fast","ppaleunyo","PPAH-reun-yoh"],["slow","neurinyo","NEU-reen-yoh"],["easy","swiwoyo","SWEE-woh-yoh"],["difficult","eoryeowoyo","UH-ryuh-woh-yoh"],["cheap","ssayo","SSAH-yoh"],["expensive","bissayo","BEE-ssah-yoh"],["clean","kkaekkeuthaeyo","KKAEK-keu-tae-yoh"],["dirty","deoreowoyo","DUH-ruh-woh-yoh"]]},{"id":"common-verbs","title":"Common verbs","items":[["to be","ida","EE-dah"],["to have / exist","itda","EET-dah"],["to go","gada","GAH-dah"],["to want","wonhada","WUHN-hah-dah"],["to eat","meokda","MUHK-dah"],["to drink","masida","MAH-shee-dah"],["to speak","malhada","MAHL-hah-dah"],["to see","boda","BOH-dah"],["to come","oda","OH-dah"],["to give","juda","JOO-dah"],["to know","alda","AHL-dah"],["to do","hada","HAH-dah"],["to like","joahada","JOH-ah-hah-dah"],["to live","salda","SAHL-dah"],["to work","ilhada","EEL-hah-dah"],["to buy","sada","SAH-dah"],["to read","ilgda","ILK-dah"],["to write","sseuda","SSEU-dah"],["to sleep","jada","JAH-dah"],["to learn","baeuda","BAE-oo-dah"],["to help","dopda","DOHP-dah"],["to need","piryohada","PEE-ryoh-hah-dah"],["to love","saranghada","SAH-rahng-hah-dah"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Korean often drops pronouns. For \"you\" it is better to use the person's name or title + -ssi, because \"dangsin\" can sound rude or intimate."],"rows":[["I (polite)","jeo","juh"],["I (informal)","na","nah"],["you (polite)","dangsin","DAHNG-sheen"],["you (informal)","neo","nuh"],["he","geu","geu"],["she","geunyeo","GEU-nyuh"],["we (polite)","jeohui","JUH-hwee"],["we (informal)","uri","OO-ree"],["they","geudeul","GEU-deul"]],"ex":[["I am a student","jeo-neun haksaeng-ieyo","juh-neun hahk-saeng-ee-eh-yoh"],["you are tall","ki-ga keoyo","kee-gah kuh-yoh"],["she is my sister","geunyeo-neun je yeodongsaeng-ieyo","GEU-nyuh-neun jeh yuh-dohng-saeng-ee-eh-yoh"],["we are friends","uri-neun chingu-yeyo","OO-ree-neun cheen-goo-yeh-yoh"],["they are teachers","geudeul-eun seonsaengnim-ieyo","GEU-deu-reun suhn-saeng-neem-ee-eh-yoh"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Korean usually does not mark the plural. Add -deul to show \"many\" (chingu → chingudeul). Numbers and context show how many."],"rows":[["friend","chingu","CHEEN-goo"],["friends","chingudeul","CHEEN-goo-deul"],["student","haksaeng","HAHK-saeng"],["students","haksaengdeul","HAHK-saeng-deul"],["counter for things","gae","gae"],["counter for people","myeong","myuhng"]],"ex":[["one friend, friends","chingu, chingudeul","CHEEN-goo CHEEN-goo-deul"],["one student, students","haksaeng, haksaengdeul","HAHK-saeng HAHK-saeng-deul"],["two people","dumyeong","doo-myuhng"],["three apples","sagwa se gae","SAH-gwah seh gae"],["five books","chaek da-seot gwon","chaek DAH-suht gwuhn"]]},{"id":"ida-to-be","title":"Ida: to be","text":["\"Ieyo\" after a consonant, \"yeyo\" after a vowel."],"rows":[["I am a student","jeo-neun haksaeng-ieyo","juh-neun hahk-saeng-ee-eh-yoh"],["it is a book","chaek-ieyo","chae-gee-eh-yoh"],["it is tea","cha-yeyo","chah-yeh-yoh"],["formal \"is\"","imnida","eem-nee-dah"],["not (is not)","...i/ga anieyo","ah-nee-eh-yoh"]],"ex":[["I am English","jeo-neun yeongguk saram-ieyo","juh-neun yuhng-gook sah-rah-mee-eh-yoh"],["he is a doctor","geu-neun uisa-yeyo","geu-neun ee-sah-yeh-yoh"],["we are tired","uri-neun pigonhaeyo","OO-ree-neun pee-gohn-hae-yoh"],["are you from Seoul?","seoul-eseo wasseoyo?","suh-oo-leh-suh wah-suh-yoh"],["they are at home","geudeul-eun jibe isseoyo","GEU-deu-reun jee-beh ee-suh-yoh"]]},{"id":"itda-to-have-to-exist","title":"Itda: to have, to exist","text":["\"Isseoyo\" = there is / I have. \"Eopseoyo\" = there is not / I do not have."],"rows":[["I have","jeo-neun ...i/ga isseoyo","ee-suh-yoh"],["there is","isseoyo","ee-suh-yoh"],["there is not","eopseoyo","uhp-suh-yoh"],["I have a car","chaga isseoyo","chah-gah ee-suh-yoh"],["I do not have time","sigani eopseoyo","shee-gah-nee uhp-suh-yoh"]],"ex":[["I have a brother","hyeong-i isseoyo","hyuh-ng-ee ee-suh-yoh"],["she has two cats","goyangi du mari isseoyo","goh-yahng-ee doo mah-ree ee-suh-yoh"],["we have time","sigan-i isseoyo","shee-gah-nee ee-suh-yoh"],["do you have a pen?","pen-i isseoyo?","pe-nee ee-suh-yoh"],["they have a car","geudeul-eun cha-ga isseoyo","GEU-deu-reun chah-gah ee-suh-yoh"]]},{"id":"regular-verbs-present-tense","title":"Regular verbs (present tense)","text":["Take the verb stem (drop -da), add -ayo or -eoyo (a / o vowel → -ayo, other vowels → -eoyo). Gada (go) → gayo, meokda (eat) → meogeoyo. Hada becomes haeyo."],"rows":[["gada (go)","gayo","gah-yoh"],["meokda (eat)","meogeoyo","muh-guh-yoh"],["hada (do)","haeyo","hae-yoh"],["ilgda (read)","ilgeoyo","il-guh-yoh"],["masida (drink)","masyeoyo","mah-shyuh-yoh"],["junbi-hada (prepare)","junbi-haeyo","joon-bee-hae-yoh"]],"ex":[["I work in a bank","jeo-neun eunhaeng-eseo ilhaeyo","juh-neun eun-haeng-eh-suh eel-hae-yoh"],["you live in Seoul","seoul-e saseyo","suh-oo-leh sah-seh-yoh"],["she reads a book","geunyeo-neun chaek-eul ilgeoyo","GEU-nyuh-neun chae-geul ik-uh-yoh"],["we learn Korean","uri-neun hangugeo-reul baeweoyo","OO-ree-neun hahn-goo-guh-reul bae-wuh-yoh"],["they buy bread","geudeul-eun ppang-eul sayo","GEU-deu-reun ppah-ngeul sah-yoh"]]},{"id":"gada-to-go","title":"Gada: to go","text":[],"rows":[["I go","gayo","gah-yoh"],["do you go?","gayo?","gah-yoh"],["let's go","gayo (let's go)","gah-yoh"],["I went","gasseoyo","gah-suh-yoh"],["I will go","gal geoyeyo","gahl guh-yeh-yoh"],["I am going","gago isseoyo","gah-goh ee-suh-yoh"]],"ex":[["I am going to school","hakgyo-e gayo","hahk-gyoh-eh gah-yoh"],["where are you going?","eodi gayo?","uh-dee gah-yoh"],["we are going home","uri-neun jibe gayo","OO-ree-neun jee-beh gah-yoh"],["she is going shopping","geunyeo-neun swopinghae gayo","GEU-nyuh-neun shoh-peeng-hae gah-yoh"],["let's go!","gayo!","gah-yoh"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["Word order is subject, object, verb (verb last). Particles mark roles: -eun/-neun (topic), -i/-ga (subject), -eul/-reul (object)."],"rows":[["subject + object + verb","Jeo-neun bap-eul meogeoyo.","juh-neun bah-beul muh-guh-yoh"],["adjective before noun","keun jip","keun jeep"],["add time or place","Jeo-neun oneul yeogi-eseo ilhaeyo.","juh-neun oh-neul yuh-gee-eh-suh eel-hae-yoh"]],"ex":[["I eat rice","jeo-neun bap-eul meogeoyo","juh-neun bah-beul muh-guh-yoh"],["Anna reads a book","Anna-neun chaek-eul ilgeoyo","AH-nah-neun chae-geul il-guh-yoh"],["we live in a big house","uri-neun keun jibe sarayo","OO-ree-neun keun jee-beh sah-rah-yoh"],["he works here today","geu-neun oneul yeogi-eseo ilhaeyo","geu-neun oh-neul yuh-gee-eh-suh eel-hae-yoh"],["the dog is black","gae-neun geomeoyo","gae-neun guh-muh-yoh"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put an before the verb (short form) or add -ji anayo to the stem (long form). Never use \"an\" with \"isseoyo\": use \"eopseoyo\"."],"rows":[["not (short)","an + verb","ahn"],["not (long)","stem + -ji anayo","jee ah-nah-yoh"],["nothing","amugeotdo","ah-moo-guht-doh"],["nobody","amudo","ah-moo-doh"],["never","jeoldae ...ji anayo","juhl-dae"]],"ex":[["I do not speak French","peurangseueo-reul an haeyo","peu-rahng-seu-uh-reul ahn hae-yoh"],["she does not live here","geunyeo-neun yeogi an sarayo","GEU-nyuh-neun yuh-gee ahn sah-rah-yoh"],["I do not want anything","amugeotdo wonhaji anayo","ah-moo-guht-doh wuhn-hah-jee ah-nah-yoh"],["nobody is here","yeogi amudo eopseoyo","yuh-gee ah-moo-doh uhp-suh-yoh"],["I never eat meat","jeoldae gogi-reul meokji anayo","juhl-dae goh-gee-reul muhk-jee ah-nah-yoh"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["A yes / no question has the same words as a statement, with rising voice. No question word is needed."],"rows":[["statement","Hangugeo-reul haeyo.","hahn-goo-guh-reul hae-yoh"],["question","Hangugeo-reul haeyo?","hahn-goo-guh-reul hae-yoh"],["do you?","...haeyo?","hae-yoh"]],"ex":[["do you speak English?","yeongeo hasil su isseoyo?","yuhng-uh hah-seel soo ee-suh-yoh"],["is she a doctor?","geunyeo-neun uisa-yeyo?","GEU-nyuh-neun ee-sah-yeh-yoh"],["do you have a pen?","pen-i isseoyo?","pe-nee ee-suh-yoh"],["are you tired?","pigonhaeyo?","pee-gohn-hae-yoh"],["is it far?","meoreoyo?","muh-ruh-yoh"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":[],"rows":[["what","mwo","mwoh"],["who","nugu","NOO-goo"],["where","eodi","UH-dee"],["when","eonje","UHN-jeh"],["why","wae","weh"],["how","eotteoke","uh-TUH-keh"],["which","eoneu","UH-neu"],["how much / how many","eolma / myeot","UHL-mah / myuht"]],"ex":[["what is this?","igeo mwoeyo?","ee-guh mwoh-eh-yoh"],["who is she?","geu yeoja-neun nugu-yeyo?","geu yuh-jah-neun noo-goo-yeh-yoh"],["where do you live?","eodi saseyo?","uh-dee sah-seh-yoh"],["when is the exam?","siheom-i eonje-eyo?","shee-huh-mee uhn-jeh-eh-yoh"],["why are you late?","wae neujeosseoyo?","weh neu-juh-suh-yoh"],["how much is it?","eolma-eyo?","uhl-mah-eh-yoh"]]},{"id":"possessives","title":"Possessives","text":["Use the pronoun + -ui, often shortened. Je = my (polite), nae = my (informal)."],"rows":[["my (polite)","je","jeh"],["my (informal)","nae","nae"],["your","dangsin-ui","DAHNG-sheen-eui"],["his","geu-ui","geu-eui"],["her","geunyeo-ui","GEU-nyuh-eui"],["our","uri","OO-ree"],["their","geudeul-ui","GEU-deu-reui"]],"ex":[["my house","je jip","jeh jeep"],["your friends","dangsin-ui chingu","DAHNG-sheen-eui CHEEN-goo"],["his sister","geu-ui yeodongsaeng","geu-eui yuh-dohng-saeng"],["our teacher","uri seonsaengnim","OO-ree suhn-saeng-neem"],["my mother","je eomma","jeh UHM-mah"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["Add -nim (title) to teachers and elders. Use -ssi after a name for equals: Minsu-ssi. Do not use -ssi to older people. Always speak politely to adults."],"rows":[["polite ending","-yo","yoh"],["formal ending","-mnida","mnee-dah"],["informal ending","(no ending)","-"],["respectful title","-nim","neem"],["after a name","-ssi","shee"]],"ex":[["hello (formal)","annyeonghasimnikka","ahn-NYUNG-hah-seem-nee-kah"],["hello (polite)","annyeonghaseyo","ahn-NYUNG-hah-seh-yoh"],["hello (informal)","annyeong","ahn-NYUNG"],["teacher (respectful)","seonsaengnim","SUHN-saeng-neem"],["thank you, Mr Kim","Kim-ssi, gamsahamnida","geem-shee gahm-sah-HAHM-nee-dah"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: stem + -ass/-eoss + eoyo. Future: stem + -l geoyeyo."],"rows":[["I went","gasseoyo","gah-suh-yoh"],["I ate","meogeosseoyo","muh-guh-suh-yoh"],["I did","haesseoyo","hae-suh-yoh"],["I will go","gal geoyeyo","gahl guh-yeh-yoh"]],"ex":[["yesterday I worked","eoje ilhaesseoyo","uh-jeh eel-hae-suh-yoh"],["she bought a book","geunyeo-neun chaek-eul sasseoyo","GEU-nyuh-neun chae-geul sah-suh-yoh"],["I went home","jibe gasseoyo","jee-beh gah-suh-yoh"],["I will call you tomorrow","naeil jeonhwa hal geoyeyo","NAE-eel juhn-hwah hahl guh-yeh-yoh"],["we will eat at eight","yeodeol si-e meogeul geoyeyo","yuh-duhl shee-eh muh-geul guh-yeh-yoh"]]}],"name":"Korean","id":"ko","badge":"Solid","note":"Written in Latin letters (no Hangul). Standard polite speech (-yo style), as spoken in Seoul. Capitals mark the stress; Korean stress is light, so say every syllable evenly."}